spec.problem:
If an answer fails, the chat stays in the generating state for good. In `send()` (src/App.tsx:220-291), the success path calls `setGenerating(false)` at line 261, but the `catch` block at lines 276-284 only flushes and dispatches `fail`. The `finally` block (285-288) clears `writingChat` and `inFlight` but never resets `generating`. So after any engine error (out of memory, or "/error" on the fake engine), `generating` stays true:
- the composer keeps showing Stop instead of Send (src/components/chat-composer.tsx:92);
- the textbox stays disabled (chat-composer.tsx:80);
- `send()` returns early at App.tsx:221.

Two side effects follow. Chats are no longer saved, because the persist effect skips while generating (App.tsx:172). The failed message also stays marked as streaming (src/components/chat.tsx:103). Only a reload resets the state.

